       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks like an error.\n\nAs written, ibuprofen 2400 mg four times daily comes to **9,600 mg/day**. That's three times the usual maximum for adults (3,200 mg/day under physician supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use). A single 2,400 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg. A dose like this raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **600 mg PO four times daily**, which is 2,400 mg/day total.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily**, which is 2,400 mg/day total.\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours**, which is a common dose for pain or fever.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. If you really do intend 2,400 mg per dose, please confirm that with your supervising resident or attending and the pharmacist first."
